Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 05:59:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] library: panorama cover shapes notify per version, not per
 map read
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every learnt ratio was written into a snapshot map. Measure read that map
for every row, and TrackPanoramaCoverShapes walked every id during
composition, so one Coil success or one prefetch put recomposed the shelf
and remeasured every lane. Prefetch also wrote the snapshot map from
Dispatchers.IO.

Learnt and committed ratios are plain maps under a lock. Measure subscribes
only to PanoramaMasonryContentEpoch, which increments when a committed
cover crosses the 0.75 band. The same band updates the committed value and
does not bump the epoch, so columns stay put. A cross-band change waits
until every visible panorama grid has been still for the existing 300 ms,
then one flush commits the batch and bumps the epoch once. Cells keep
their own float state and read that epoch; onSuccess updates the cell only
when the band did not change. Snapshot writes run on the owner thread.
IO only decodes bounds and reads or writes the same text file.

The file is app-layer and has a counterpart in anikku-harmony. There the constant is named RatioSwitchToPanorama.

与 anikku-harmony 0034 同源。
